From 405c670bbba98d51a4767378fe1cf474427c321e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri John Ledkov <dimitri.ledkov@surgut.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:35:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Chainguard Cryptographic Hardening

Add configure options to compile out legacy and unused cryptography,
and make the PKINIT key exchange default to P-384.

* --disable-des3 removes the des3-cbc-sha1 and des3-cbc-raw enctypes
  and the hmac-sha1-des3 checksum type.
* --disable-rc4 removes the arcfour-hmac and arcfour-hmac-exp enctypes,
  MD4, and the HMAC-MD5 checksum types.  The S4U2Self client then sends
  only PA-S4U-X509-USER, as PA-FOR-USER requires an HMAC-MD5 checksum.
  Plain MD5 remains for GSS-API channel bindings (RFC 4121) and RADIUS,
  and plain HMAC-MD5 remains for the RADIUS Message-Authenticator.
* --disable-camellia removes the camellia128-cts-cmac and
  camellia256-cts-cmac enctypes and their CMAC checksum types.

Compiled-out primitives are omitted from libk5crypto entirely, so it
neither contains nor uses OpenSSL's DES, RC4, MD4, Camellia, or CMAC
implementations.  krb5int_arcfour_gsscrypt() remains as a stub returning
KRB5_BAD_ENCTYPE for libgssapi_krb5.  Disabled enctypes are still named
(by their shortest names) when displayed.

Change PKINIT_DEFAULT_DH_MIN_BITS from 2048-bit MODP to P-384, for both
the client group choice and the KDC minimum.

Make the C and Python test suites skip vectors and test passes for
compiled-out enctypes, exporting have_des3, have_rc4, and have_camellia
to k5test.  Update t_pkinit.py for the P-384 default, and only test the
finite-field groups when OpenSSL provides them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
